From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Bifrost <bifrost@local>
Date: Tue, 29 Apr 2026 13:50:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] bifrost: SHMEM data plane (Phases 1-5 + ringbuf wrap)

Consolidated bifrost kernel patch for the SHMEM data plane.

Files patched:
  - kernel/bpf/helpers.c: bifrost helpers + six BPF kfuncs
    (current_exe_path, emit_vma_table, publish_vma_table,
    shmem_reserve, shmem_submit, shmem_kick) +
    bifrost_set_shmem_ringbuf + bifrost_set_doorbell_callback.
  - rust/bindings/bindings_helper.h: bindgen externs.
  - kernel/bpf/verifier.c: bifrost_kfunc_shmem_reserve in
    special_kfunc_set/list with PTR_TO_MEM return-handling.

This update adds wraparound to bifrost_kfunc_shmem_reserve.
Previously a record that would cross end-of-buffer caused the
reserve to fail, dropping records on long-running sessions.
Now: when a record won't fit before end, atomically claim the
remaining bytes as a "padding record" with
BIFROST_RB_FLAG_PADDING set and continue past the wrap. The
consumer recognizes the flag and skips the full claimed length.

Verified: 23 929 records over 9 seconds (~1.37 K rec/s) through
~2× wraps of the 6 MB ringbuf, zero rejections or invalid-size
errors. Padding records skipped silently as designed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
